#3984
The Ocean Floor~
   As you walk along the murky bottom of the ocean, all thoughts of the
prospect of adventure and riches esacpe your mind completely, leaving only the
feelings of death and fear to weave their twisted web upon your soul.  You
cannot even see the hands you hold up in front of your face in the total
darkness of this forboding water.  Then suddenly, you feel something brush up
against your leg, and you realize: You're not alone.    
~
